---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PolicyContact from "../../components/PolicyContact.astro";
import { brand } from "../../../brand.config";
import { resolveLocale, useTranslations } from "@/i18n/ui";

const t = useTranslations(resolveLocale(Astro.currentLocale));
---

<BaseLayout title={t("Policies.privacyTitle")}>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <div class="page-shell__inner">
      <h1>{t("Policies.privacyTitle")}</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: September 2026</em></p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how {brand.name} ("we" or "the Site")
        collects, uses, and discloses your personal information when you visit or
        use our website ({brand.siteUrl}), contact us, or interact with our B2B
        wholesale children's watch services (collectively, the "Services"). This
        policy applies to website visitors, wholesale buyers, OEM/ODM project
        clients, and anyone whose information we collect under this Privacy Policy
        ("you").
      </p>
      <p>Please read this Privacy Policy carefully.</p>

      <hr />

      <h2>Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in
        our practices or for operational, legal, or regulatory reasons. We will post
        the revised Privacy Policy on the Site, update the "Last updated" date, and
        take any other steps required by applicable law to inform you of these
        changes.
      </p>

      <h2>How we collect and use your personal information</h2>
      <p>
        To provide the Services, we collect personal information from various
        sources as outlined below. The information we collect and how we use it may
        vary depending on how you interact with us — for example, requesting a quote
        for ready-stock watches, starting an OEM/ODM customization project, or
        communicating via WhatsApp, email, or our contact form. In addition to the
        uses listed below, we may use the information we collect to communicate with
        you, improve our Services, comply with legal obligations, enforce our terms,
        and protect or defend our Services, rights, and those of our users and
        others.
      </p>

      <h2>What personal information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        The types of personal information we collect depend on how you interact with
        our Site and use our Services.
      </p>

      <h3>Information we collect directly from you</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Contact information: your name, company name, address, phone number, and
          email address.
        </li>
        <li>
          Order information: billing and shipping addresses, payment confirmation,
          model numbers, quantities, MOQ details, and delivery preferences for
          ready-stock or wholesale orders.
        </li>
        <li>
          Business information: importer or distributor details, tax or registration
          information, and destination-country import requirements when relevant to
          your order.
        </li>
        <li>
          OEM/ODM project information: brand assets, logos, dial or case designs,
          packaging artwork, customization specifications, samples, and other
          materials you provide for custom watch production.
        </li>
        <li>
          Customer support information: messages, photos, videos, and other content
          you send via our contact form, email, WhatsApp, or other channels.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Information we collect about your usage</h3>
      <p>
        We may automatically collect certain information about your interaction with
        the Services ("Usage Data"), such as through cookies, pixels, and similar
        technologies. Usage Data may include device information, browser information,
        network connection details, IP addresses, pages viewed, and other
        information about how you use the Site. We use privacy-focused analytics
        tools to understand traffic and improve the website.
      </p>

      <h3>Information we obtain from third parties</h3>
      <p>
        We may obtain information about you from third parties, including vendors
        and service providers who collect information on our behalf (for example,
        payment processors, shipping carriers, or email delivery partners).
      </p>

      <h2>How we use your personal information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Providing products and services: to respond to inquiries, prepare quotes,
          process ready-stock wholesale orders, manage OEM/ODM production, arrange
          shipping and tracking, handle quality claims, and fulfill our agreement
          with you.
        </li>
        <li>
          Marketing and communications: to send B2B updates about new models,
          factory capabilities, or promotions where permitted, and to follow up on
          your inquiries. You may opt out of non-essential marketing messages at
          any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          Security and fraud prevention: to detect, investigate, or take action
          regarding potentially fraudulent, illegal, or malicious activity.
        </li>
        <li>
          Communicating with you and service improvement: to provide customer
          support, improve our website and catalog, and understand how buyers use
          our Services.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Use of cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Our website uses cookies and similar technologies to operate the Site,
        remember preferences, and understand usage through analytics. You can remove
        or reject cookies through your browser settings, but some features may not
        work as intended. We do not use cookies to sell your personal data.
      </p>

      <h2>How we disclose personal information</h2>
      <p>
        We may disclose your personal information to third parties in certain
        circumstances, such as:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          To vendors or service providers that perform services on our behalf (for
          example, payment processing, email delivery, shipping and logistics,
          analytics, hosting, and IT support).
        </li>
        <li>
          In response to legal obligations, court orders, or to enforce our terms,
          protect our rights, or the rights of our users or others.
        </li>
        <li>
          To affiliates or partners involved in fulfilling your order, such as freight
          forwarders or customs brokers, when necessary for delivery.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third-party websites and links</h2>
      <p>
        Our Site may include links to third-party websites or platforms (for
        example, social media or payment pages). If you follow links to sites not
        controlled by us, you should review their privacy policies and terms. We are
        not responsible for the privacy practices or security of such sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's data</h2>
      <p>
        Our Services are intended for business buyers and are not directed at
        children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If
        you are a parent or guardian and believe a child has provided us with
        personal information, please contact us to request deletion.
      </p>

      <h2>Security and retention of your information</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable security measures to protect your personal information,
        but no method of transmission or storage is completely secure. We retain
        personal information as needed to respond to inquiries, fulfill orders
        (including OEM/ODM project records), comply with legal obligations, resolve
        disputes, and enforce our agreements. Custom project files and order records
        may be kept for a reasonable period after completion.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your location, you may have some or all of the following rights
        regarding your personal information:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Right to access: you may request access to personal information we hold
          about you.
        </li>
        <li>
          Right to delete: you may request that we delete your personal information,
          subject to legal and contractual retention requirements.
        </li>
        <li>
          Right to correct: you may request that we correct inaccurate personal
          information we hold about you.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Additional rights may apply under local law. To exercise these rights or ask
        questions about this policy, please contact us using the details below.
      </p>

      <PolicyContact />

      <p class="policy-related">
        Related:{" "}
        <a href="/policies/terms-of-service">Terms of service</a> ·{" "}
        <a href="/policies/shipping-tax">Shipping &amp; tax</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
